.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-attach 1  "attach 0.6.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-attach \- Re\-attach this terminal to a session that is already running
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh attach\fR [\fB\-\-escape\-char\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-screen\-sync\fR] [\fB\-\-predict\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-status\-line\fR] [\fB\-A \fR] [\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-a \fR] [\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-J \fR] [\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-punch\fR] [\fB\-\-rendezvous\fR] [\fB\-\-jump\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fISESSION_REF\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Re\-attach this terminal to a session that is already running.
.PP
Only possible from the device that opened the session, whose resume credential is bound to it (`docs/CLI.md` §6.2, §7). Detach with the escape sequence `~d`; the session keeps running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-escape\-char\fR \fI<CHAR>\fR
Escape character for the line\-start detach sequences, or `none`. Default `~`; only active when stdin is a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-screen\-sync\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Screen state sync: `auto` (default), `on` (require it) or `off` (plain byte stream). See `qsh \-\-help`
.TP
\fB\-\-predict\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Local echo prediction: `auto` (default), `always` or `never`. See `qsh \-\-help`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-status\-line\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Link\-status line: `on` (default) or `off`. See `qsh \-\-help`
.TP
\fB\-A\fR
Forward the local ssh\-agent to the host for this command (ADR\-0055). Only listing keys and signing reach your agent. With `\-a`, the last one given wins
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ssh\fR
Never run ssh on this command\*(Aqs behalf: no automatic bootstrap of an unknown name, and no restarting of a pinned host\*(Aqs serve over ssh when the connection fails (`docs/CLI.md` §7). `qsh pair ssh` is not affected; it is ssh by definition
.TP
\fB\-a\fR
Do not forward the agent for this command, even when `[agent].forward = "yes"`
.TP
\fB\-\-install\-remote\fR
When the ssh bootstrap finds no `qsh` on the remote host (or one too old to answer it), install this machine\*(Aqs release into `~/.local/bin` there without asking (`docs/CLI.md` §7). Works with `\-\-json`
.TP
\fB\-J\fR \fI<HOPS>\fR
Reach the host through these pinned peers for this command, `ssh \-J` spelled: `a` or `a,b`, or `none` to go the ordinary way (ADR\-0056). Same as `\-\-jump`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\-remote\fR
Never install or upgrade `qsh` on the remote host, and do not ask; a missing `qsh` ends as `remote_qsh_missing`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-punch\fR
Never start a hole punch on this command\*(Aqs behalf, and send no `PunchRequest` (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0054 decision 19). The route is the direct dial alone. Wins over `[punch].mode`
.TP
\fB\-\-rendezvous\fR \fI<PEER>\fR
Use this pinned peer as the rendezvous for hole punching on this command, instead of the host\*(Aqs own `rendezvous` hints (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0054 decision 4). Must be pinned with an address. Not stored
.TP
\fB\-\-jump\fR \fI<HOPS>\fR
Reach the host through these pinned peers, first hop first, for this command: `a` or `a,b` (`docs/CLI.md` §7, ADR\-0056 decision 20). Each hop is the name of a pin; a `user@` or `:port` on it is ignored by the QUIC path. `none` goes the ordinary way even when the host\*(Aqs pin has a `jump`. Wins over `\-o ProxyJump` and over the pin\*(Aqs own `jump`. Not stored. The short `\-J` is the same flag on the commands that take it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fISESSION_REF\fR>
Opaque session handle (`<host>/<session_id>`) from `session open` or `sessions`
.SH VERSION
v0.6.0
